# What's new — shown once per installed version in the app.
# One `## <version>` section per release; the lines below it are the notes.
# Keep the matching full entry in the repository's CHANGELOG.md.

## 3.6.0
- Fixed: tags.yaml is now read as a plain list (`- tag` per line, as written by dataset_autotag.py), so the tag bar shows every tag. A nested `tags:` key is ignored and saving rewrites the file as a plain list.

## 3.5.0
- Settings > Shortcuts now has an Edit view: click a binding and press the new key combination, then Save. Changes are written to your own shortcuts.txt (the shipped one is left alone), and a reset button restores the default.

## 3.4.2
- Fixed: on a fresh install the Load a dataset, What's new and Tip of the day dialogs no longer appear at the same time; they now show one after another.

## 3.4.1
- Fixed: the installer now reliably creates the ybe alias even when a stale ybe symlink or directory is already in the launcher folder.

## 3.4.0
- A daily tip dialog now suggests one random feature each day.
- New built-in update_tags action (run after save by a shipped on_after_save hook) adds new tag names to tags.yaml on demand.
- Per-dataset Tags folder setting; the tag bar warns when a tag is missing from tags.yaml.
- Settings > View is now Settings > General, with a Show tip on start toggle; the README is a lighter quick start with docs/ for details.
- Fixed: choosing All splits no longer snaps back to the previously selected split. The last image is now remembered per split.

## 3.3.0
- UI settings (View/Layout, panel sizes, floating-window positions) are saved on the server too, so a new browser starts with your setup. A value you change in a browser still wins there.

## 3.2.0
- Settings > Layout now has a block per widget with a Show toggle and a Location selector.
- Tags are visible by default; the old View > Tags switch is gone.

## 3.1.0
- Actions, Navigation (Prev / counter / Next) and Save / Undo are now dockable widgets like Tags and Boxes.
- The bottom panel hides when it holds no widget; the box list no longer adds inner padding.

## 3.0.0
- Updates are done with `ybe update` (alias `ybe upgrade`); `ybx.sh` is only the installer. The launchers are always added to ~/.local/bin (the `--no-link` option is gone).

## 2.16.0
- Tags and Boxes are now dockable widgets: send them to the left, right or bottom panel, or keep them floating. A panel only appears while it holds a widget.

## 2.13.0
- Releases for major/minor version bumps are now tagged and published automatically on GitHub.

## 2.12.0
- Added `ybx.sh uninstall` / `ybe uninstall`: removes the app, venv and launchers but keeps your files; `--purge --yes` removes the whole folder.

## 2.11.0
- Added `ybx.sh update --latest` (newest commit on main) and `ybx.sh update --commit <sha>`; both work over HTTP without git.

## 2.10.0
- `ybx.sh install` / `upgrade` now start the app automatically (background) and restart a running instance; use `--no-start` to skip.

## 2.9.0
- New Layout settings: choose the panel side (left/right) and detach Tags or Boxes into movable floating windows.
- Float windows snap to a screen edge on release (or use the L/T/R/B buttons); their position is remembered.

## 2.8.0
- Added a first-run "Load a dataset" dialog: paste a data.yaml path and click Load.
- Settings now uses tabs (View / Dataset / Shortcuts / Updates); the dataset dropdown, path input and Load button sit on one row.
- Replaced the breaking-change warnings with a "What's new" changelog, shown once after the app updates to a new version.
- `ybe check-update` no longer prints the `breaking_changes:` and `breaking_notes:` lines.
